 34SI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34SI dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 12-Jun-2026)          
 34SI c  2024Lu03: {+34}Al ions were produced via reactions of a 480-MeV 14-|mA 
 34SI2c  proton beam impinging on a 9.89-g/cm{+2} UC{-x} target at ISAC, TRIUMF.
 34SI3c  The ions were selectively ionized using the TRIUMF Resonant Ionization 
 34SI4c  Laser Ion Source (TRILIS), accelerated to 40 keV, separated by the ISAC
 34SI5c  mass separator, and delivered to a movable Mylar tape. The deexciting  
 34SI6c  |g rays were detected using the Gamma-Ray Infrastructure For           
 34SI7c  Fundamental Investigations of Nuclei (GRIFFIN) Ge array, consisting of 
 34SI8c  16 Compton-suppressed HPGe clover detectors. |b particles were detected
 34SI9c  using the Scintillating Electron Positron Tagging ARray (SCEPTAR),     
 34SIAc  consisting of ten plastic scintillator paddles and a 1-mm-thin, fast   
 34SIBc  plastic scintillator called the zero degree scintillator (ZDS).        
 34SICc  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g(|q), |b|g-coin, and |g|g-coin. Deduced J, |p,  
 34SIDc  decay branching ratios, log {Ift}. Comparisons with shell-model        
 34SIEc  calculations using the FSU interaction Hamiltonian.                    
